mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif; font-size: 14pt;">Health Services Management is a discipline that studies how to rationally allocate, distribute, and utilize limited health resources, enhance social and economic benefits, and improve population health levels by applying modern management science theories and methods based on the objectives, functions, and fundamental principles of health systems. Its main contents include the nature of health services and health work policies, the health organizational system, medical security systems, health planning management, health resource management, health service administration, health performance evaluation, and health status assessment, etc.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
